# Configuration

Use this pattern for typed settings in host and library projects.

## Configuration Types

- Name typed settings records `XConfiguration`, not `XOptions`.
- Use `sealed record` types with PascalCase properties and sensible defaults.
- Expose a public `SectionName` constant when the type maps to an `appsettings.json` section.
- Place configuration types under a `Configuration/` folder in the owning project or feature area.
- Keep one configuration type per file; the file name must match the type name.
- Mark required settings with `[Required]` from `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations`.
- Properties without `[Required]` keep their record defaults when the setting is missing.

## appsettings.json

- Use PascalCase top-level section names (`SoongHost`, `Ollama`, `Logging`).
- Group related settings under nested objects when a feature owns multiple values.
- Keep baseline values in `appsettings.json`.
- Support environment overlays, user secrets, and environment variables through `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication`.
- Pass section names as parameters during registration; do not hard-code section names inside services.

## Generic Loader

- Use `LTs.Configurations.Configurations.TypedConfigurationLoader` for loading and Autofac registration.
- Do not use `IConfigurationSection.Get<T>()` object binding for typed configuration records.
- Do not create per-type loader classes when the generic loader is sufficient.
- Use `LoadConfiguration<T>( IConfiguration configuration, string sectionName )` to load a typed record from a section.
- Use `AddConfiguration<T>( ContainerBuilder builder, string sectionName )` to register a typed record as an Autofac singleton.
- Use the `AddConfiguration<T>( ..., Func<T, T>? configure )` overload for post-load transforms such as environment-variable expansion.
- Required-property failures must throw `ConfigurationException` with the full section path, for example `SoongHost:Model`.

```csharp
builder.AddConfiguration<SoongHostConfiguration>(
    SoongHostConfiguration.SectionName,
    configuration => configuration with
    {
        WorkingDirectory = Environment.ExpandEnvironmentVariables( configuration.WorkingDirectory )
    } );

builder.AddConfiguration<OllamaConfiguration>( OllamaConfiguration.SectionName );
```

## Host Registration

- Chain all host configuration registration inside `Program.RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )`.
- Never create a separate `ConfigurationIoC.cs` or equivalent configuration bootstrap class.
- Register logging configuration with `RegisterLogConfiguration( sectionName )` from `Program.RegisterConfiguration`.
- Call `AddConfiguration<T>` from `Program.RegisterConfiguration` with explicit section names.
- Pass `RegisterConfiguration` directly to `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication`; do not delegate configuration registration to another type.

```csharp
builder.ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>(
    string.Empty,
    RegisterConfiguration,
    RegisterServices,
    RegisterWebServices );

internal static void RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )
{
    builder.RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" );
    builder.AddConfiguration<SoongHostConfiguration>( SoongHostConfiguration.SectionName );
    builder.AddConfiguration<OllamaConfiguration>( OllamaConfiguration.SectionName );
}
```

## Service Registration

- Keep runtime service registration in `DependencyInjection/` extension methods named `Add<Area>...`.
- Resolve typed configuration inside service registration with `IAutofacConfigurationProvider.Get<T>()`.
- Do not bind typed configuration through `IServiceCollection.Configure<T>()` in host projects.
- Register runtime singletons in Autofac, not ad hoc MS.DI registrations in `Program`.

## Testing

- Add tests in `LTs.Configurations.test` for generic loader behavior when changing loader rules.
- Add host tests that verify `Program.RegisterConfiguration` resolves expected typed configuration.
- Add tests for `[Required]` failures with clear `ConfigurationException` messages.
- Group test methods in `#region` blocks named after the production method or API under test (for example `#region LoadConfiguration`, `#region AddConfiguration`).
- Build test configuration with `AddJsonString()` instead of `AddInMemoryCollection()`.
